Unused-declaration diagnostics: add info/hint levels and the LSP Unnecessary tag (+ VS Code setting)

Requested 2026-08-29 by Max: make the uncalled/unused warning quieter, like
an info message, and support it in the VS Code extension too.

## Why / LSP background
Two independent mechanisms exist:
- `DiagnosticSeverity::INFORMATION` (3) / `HINT` (4) — standard.
- `DiagnosticTag::UNNECESSARY` (1) — the idiomatic "unused" signal; clients
  fade/grey the range regardless of severity (VS Code gates on
  `editor.showUnused`). TypeScript uses HINT + UNNECESSARY for "declared but
  never read", which is why unused vars grey out without filling Problems.

Client behaviour that drives the choice:
- INFORMATION → listed in the VS Code Problems panel, blue underline.
- HINT → NOT listed in Problems; editor-only subtle underline.
- UNNECESSARY tag → the grey-out, orthogonal to severity.

## Current state
- `UnusedLevel { Ignore, Warn, Error }` (src/config.rs:183), severity map in
  `unused_severity` (src/server/diagnostics.rs:175).
- `unused` already resolves through the whole ladder: TOML
  (src/config.rs:879), user config (src/user_config.rs:314),
  initializationOptions (src/config.rs:1045).
- Quiet severities already render: src/cli/pretty.rs:146-147 (colour, counted
  as `n_other`), src/cli/watch.rs:443-444 (TUI Severity::Info/Hint),
  src/main.rs:245-247 (already excluded from the failing exit code).

Gaps:
- `grep -rn DiagnosticTag src` is empty — every diagnostic leaves
  `tags: None` via `..Default::default()` (src/server/diagnostics.rs:203).
  lsp-types 0.94.1 has `DiagnosticTag::UNNECESSARY`.
- The extension has no `unused` setting; settings.ts forwards only
  openplanet_dir, plugins_dir, game_target, signature_mode, defines,
  plugin_roots.

## Plan
1. Add `Info` and `Hint` to `UnusedLevel`. Aliases: info/information/note →
   Info; hint/faded/grey/gray → Hint. Default stays `Warn` (no behaviour
   change for existing users).
2. Attach `DiagnosticTag::UNNECESSARY` to unused diagnostics at EVERY level
   (including warn/error) — that is what produces the grey-out and what makes
   `hint` readable rather than invisible. No client-capability gate needed:
   the server does not retain client capabilities and clients without
   `publishDiagnostics.tagSupport` ignore the field.
3. Extension: `openplanetLsp.unused` enum (ignore/hint/info/warn/error) with
   an explicit unset default, forwarded as `unused` — honouring the existing
   "only forward what the user set" contract (settings.ts:1-10) so a repo
   `.openplanet-lsp.toml` keeps control.
4. Docs: README config table, `src/user_config.rs:314` choices list, both
   CHANGELOGs.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Server/config (Rust):
- `unused_level_parse_accepts_canonical_and_alias_variants` extended: every
  new alias parses; unknown tokens still `None`.
- severity map: Ignore→None, Hint→HINT, Info→INFORMATION, Warn→WARNING,
  Error→ERROR (table-driven over all five).
- tag present at every emitting level; `Ignore` still emits nothing.
- ladder round-trip per level: TOML key, user config, initializationOptions
  (`{"unused": "hint"}`), and the TOML bool forms (`true`→Warn,
  `false`→Ignore) unchanged.
- generalise over declaration kinds (function / local / global / class /
  enum) so the tag+severity apply uniformly, not just to functions.
- CLI: `check` exit code stays 0 at hint/info even without
  `--warnings-as-errors`, and `--warnings-as-errors` does NOT promote
  hint/info (only WARNING) — guards main.rs:245-247.
- pretty output counts hint/info as `n_other`, not as warnings.

Extension (vitest, pure `buildInitializationOptions`):
- unset / empty → no `unused` key (repo TOML keeps control).
- each of ignore/hint/info/warn/error → forwarded verbatim.
- invalid value → not forwarded (mirrors isValidGameTarget/SignatureMode).